{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI write from Breda, weary but content. This morning I walked four hours in Antwerp with Mr. van Ghert. The churches here rival Ghent’s, filled with life-size marbles and dozens of great canvases by Rubens and van Dyck. It is a sight that stirs the soul, though I confess my legs feel it more than my mind.\n\nWe parted there. Van Ghert returns to Brussels to seek your letters and forward them to Amsterdam. I trust you are well, and that Karl and Immanuel are settling into their routines. I think of you constantly, and of the quiet of our home in Berlin. The journey continues, but my heart remains with you.\n\nGive my regards to the household. I shall write again when I have news of your correspondence.\n\nYours ever,\n\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795218852,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":182,"prompt_tokens":945,"total_tokens":1127,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-HfWddEqaXKyxj6UQd0W0Q1NC85j5FZcj","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":945,"prompt_ms":947.507,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.00265291005291,"prompt_per_second":997.3541092572403,"predicted_n":182,"predicted_ms":4347.139,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.017342541436467,"predicted_per_second":41.63657982871033}}